                      that stood here explained the bulletin's column shapes to
                      a reader who had come to see what the town is asking —
                      this build's problem, told as if it were theirs. The
                      DISTINCTION is what had to survive the shortening, and it
                      does: a quest the daily mirror cannot measure says so
                      neutrally rather than showing a zero it did not earn.

                      THE COMMENT LIVES OUT HERE, as a JSX comment rather than a
                      block comment inside the ternary, and that is mechanical:
                      the content laws in test/civic-hub.test.mjs strip JSX
                      comments before asking "is this struck sentence still on
                      the page", and a bare block comment in an expression
                      position is invisible to that stripper — so quoting the
                      struck line there turned the removal's own falsifier red
                      about a page that was already correct. */}
                  {q.done != null && q.of ? (
                    <div class="m-bar-wrap">
                      <div class="m-bar" role="img" aria-label={`${q.done} of ${q.of} residents finished this today`}>
