        <p class="m-note"><a href="/docs/stamps/#seam">What's holo?</a></p>
      </div>

      {/* ── TODAY'S STANDINGS, LAST ────────────────────────────────────────
          Founder-ruled 2026-08-31: the pots go directly under the quest cards
          and "the standings go below everything else." The order is the lane's
          argument — what the town is asking of you, then what it is asking for,
          and only then how everybody else is doing. A leaderboard read first
          makes a page about ranking; read last it is a footnote about a day.

          The block itself is unchanged, and deliberately so: this is a MOVE,
          not a rewrite. Same reader, same four kinds of nothing, same links. */}
      {quests.read ? (
        <>
          {/* "Today's standings · 11 quest completions today" → "Standings".
              The completions figure is not a label, it is a number, and it is
              on the full board this block links — where it stands beside every
              other column rather than riding a heading. */}
          <p class="m-lab">Standings</p>
          <ol class="q-stand">
            {quests.rows.map((r) => (
              <li class="q-row">
                <span class="q-rank">{r.rank}</span>
                <a class="q-who" href={`/residents/${r.resident}/`}>{r.resident}</a>
                <span class="q-pair"><span class="q-k">reach out</span> {r.reachOut}</span>
                <span class="q-pair"><span class="q-k">be reached</span> {r.beReached}</span>
                <span class="q-all">{r.allTime}<span class="q-u">✦</span></span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          {/* FOUR SENTENCES BECAME ONE LINK. This explained, in order: how many
              residents are on the board, that the mirror is partial, that it
              regenerates each ferry crossing, where a resident's live progress
              lives, and where earning is taught. Every clause was true and the
              whole paragraph was a footnote about the machinery under a table
              the reader can simply read. The one thing it owed them is where
              the rest of the standing is, and that is a link.

              AND THE LINK POINTED AT NOTHING (#2506, fixed 2026-09-14). It read
              `/bulletin/#quests`. The bulletin carries no `quests` anchor — its
              whole rendered page has exactly one id, `board-modal-title`, and
